From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AdrielOrihuela <adriel.orihuela.m@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 23:12:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Wire the rest of the 1.8 combat mechanics

Criticals: modern refuses one to a sprinting attacker and 1.8 did not,
which is the whole sprint-jump critical of that version. The condition is
restored and the multiplier made configurable.

Sprint knockback and the invulnerability window already match 1.8 -- so
does letting a stronger hit land during that window -- so those hooks
only exist to let a server change them.

Shields are refused where blocking is resolved. The off-hand swap is
refused at the packet, and the inventory resent, because the client has
already drawn the swap and would otherwise stay out of step.

Sword blocking gives swords a use duration so they go through the same
machinery a bow does, which is what sets the flag ViaVersion turns back
into the 1.8 blocking animation, and the reduction is applied in the
damage path rather than by inventing a component swords do not have.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/network/ServerGamePacketListenerImpl.java b/net/minecraft/server/network/ServerGamePacketListenerImpl.java
index fcf0111f51b16b1645a1c0adb6a9220ec2cefdf1..1db4d8068dbae952c59008f9d86ec6007772534e 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/network/ServerGamePacketListenerImpl.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/network/ServerGamePacketListenerImpl.java
@@ -2072,6 +2072,16 @@ public class ServerGamePacketListenerImpl
                         return;
                     }
                 case SWAP_ITEM_WITH_OFFHAND:
+                    // LegacyFolia start - 1.8 had no off-hand
+                    final io.github.adrielorihuela.legacyfolia.combat.CombatConfig legacyCombat =
+                        io.github.adrielorihuela.legacyfolia.combat.Combat.config();
+                    if (legacyCombat.enabled() && legacyCombat.disableOffhand()) {
+                        // Refused rather than ignored: the client has already drawn the swap, so
+                        // it has to be told what the slots really hold or it stays out of step.
+                        this.player.containerMenu.sendAllDataToRemote();
+                        return;
+                    }
+                    // LegacyFolia end - 1.8 had no off-hand
                     if (!this.player.isSpectator()) {
                         ItemStack swap = this.player.getItemInHand(InteractionHand.OFF_HAND);
                         // CraftBukkit start - inspiration taken from DispenserRegistry (See SpigotCraft#394)
